Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.73,0:00:06.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Welcome home, Father!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.14,0:00:09.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm home, Selim.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.22,0:00:18.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Here.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.26,0:00:24.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can go ahead and open it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.91,0:00:25.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.68,0:00:33.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thank you very much!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.34,0:00:37.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Happy tenth birthday, Selim.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.39,0:00:41.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where are we?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.99,0:00:44.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're at you-know-who's place.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.92,0:00:46.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"You-know-who"?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.17,0:00:49.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The one who is making you homunculi search for the Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.21,0:00:50.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's not all.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.86,0:00:55.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The one who found us, \Nbrought us together, and nurtured us.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.44,0:00:58.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're being tricked—all you homunculi who want to become human.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.27,0:01:01.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those who are being tricked are fools.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.82,0:01:03.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What about you?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.60,0:01:05.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.46,0:01:08.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That person just wants the \NPhilosopher's Stone to use personally.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.72,0:01:11.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So what?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.15,0:01:15.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As long as I get to see humans suffer, \Nthat's good enough for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.93,0:01:22.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, now, your body is precious.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.47,0:01:24.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't do anything reckless.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.71,0:01:26.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shoot!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.98,0:01:33.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How many people do you think Scar killed to make you the Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.99,0:01:36.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Of the soldiers who \Ncharged into Liore,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.07,0:01:38.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,seven thousand of them \Ndisappeared in an instant.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.79,0:01:40.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They're not dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.91,0:01:42.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They're all right here.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.24,0:01:47.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh yeah, and the guys that died long ago in Ishbal who were in Scar's right arm
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.75,0:01:49.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,are locked away \Ninside there as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.92,0:01:52.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Awesome, awesome!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.26,0:01:56.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've got thousands—tens of thousands—of lives there inside you.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.29,0:01:58.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We should put them \Nto good use, huh?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.31,0:02:08.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I should have died.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.60,0:02:11.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Back then...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.87,0:02:13.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and back then...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.33,0:02:15.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and back then too.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.32,0:02:20.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So then, why am I still alive?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.40,0:02:22.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.17,0:02:25.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dad?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.93,0:02:29.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.98,0:02:35.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those who obtain it are set free from the Law of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.56,0:02:39.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is no need to pay a price \Nin order to obtain something, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.51,0:02:44.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We sought it and found it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.37,0:04:36.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.94,0:04:39.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What were you doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.35,0:04:42.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry. Is this the place?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.53,0:04:45.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes. This is definitely the place.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.10,0:04:47.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Show me one more time.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.85,0:04:54.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dad once came here to Central, \Nlooking for a way to refine the red water.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.92,0:04:59.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He wound up going to a place called the 5th Laboratory,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.46,0:05:02.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and there, he met up \Nwith a certain alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.81,0:05:09.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That person told him that there was some indispensable element
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.40,0:05:12.87,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,that was necessary to transmute the red water \Nall the way into a Philosopher's Stone
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.87,0:05:15.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and hinted to him \Nthat it was human lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.52,0:05:18.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He also showed him \Nwhere the real laboratory was.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.42,0:05:24.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The 5th Laboratory was nothing more than a secret entrance.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.00,0:05:27.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In fact, there was an even larger human experimentation lab.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.72,0:05:31.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This does indeed appear to be the place that we have been searching for.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.15,0:05:34.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.76,0:05:38.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But Al-kun is in danger, \Nthough we don't know what kind, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.34,0:05:43.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's all right. He's just \Ngotten a little lost. That's all.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.12,0:05:48.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.72,0:05:54.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The reason why we showed you what was in this journal...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.18,0:05:56.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,was not because we wanted you to make a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.84,0:06:02.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know. I'm not going there \Nto create a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.01,0:06:03.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Believe me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.73,0:06:16.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come back to us now!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.65,0:06:18.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come back to us alive!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.20,0:06:34.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,According to Dad's journal,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.11,0:06:36.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,you descend from the temple of the ancient religion
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.52,0:06:39.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and go farther and farther underground, \Nand then suddenly...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.29,0:06:46.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,there's another city, \Nall tucked away beneath Central.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.68,0:06:49.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dad said that judging by its style of architecture,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.99,0:06:52.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it looked like the city was nearly four hundred years old.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.77,0:06:56.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a legend that says \Nthat the city that was there,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.24,0:06:58.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,where Central is now, \Nvanished overnight.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.27,0:07:04.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dad says he thought that there might have been alchemists who were performing
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.37,0:07:09.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,some kind of experiment and may have closed up the whole city underground.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.09,0:07:14.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The people of the city \Nwere all sacrificed
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.91,0:07:17.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,to be used in their \NPhilosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.85,0:07:21.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And then, to hide the fact that there weren't any people left,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.86,0:07:24.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,they made the city itself disappear.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.00,0:07:28.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's actually someone who thought that up?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.13,0:07:31.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is anyone there?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.24,0:07:38.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know you're here! You knew about everything, didn't you,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.56,0:07:41.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Pop?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.58,0:07:49.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, Gluttony.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.83,0:07:51.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Be patient.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.54,0:07:57.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This girl's body is \Nvery important, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.01,0:08:05.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So pretty. It's no wonder why Ed and Al would like you.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.97,0:08:09.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They {\i1}are{\i0} his children.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.26,0:08:11.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, what happened to Lust?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.26,0:08:14.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, what could have \Nhappened to her?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.59,0:08:17.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right, I need to \Nget my dress ready.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.20,0:08:20.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We have to be pretty \Nwhen we greet him.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.18,0:08:22.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Somebody's here.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.35,0:08:25.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My, that was quick.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.89,0:08:28.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where is he?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.04,0:08:29.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wrath...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.04,0:08:29.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where is he?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.92,0:08:31.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What a pest!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.54,0:08:32.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where's the Philosopher's Stone?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.32,0:08:33.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the meaning of this?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.43,0:08:35.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where is he?! Where did he go?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.30,0:08:35.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I thought he was keeping an eye on Edward.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.16,0:08:38.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Tell me, Envy! Please!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.95,0:08:38.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's what I thought I told him to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.33,0:08:40.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please! Give me the \NPhilosopher's Stone, quick!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.41,0:08:44.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wrath, you have to be a good boy, \Nor I won't make you human.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.35,0:08:45.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no time for that!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.92,0:08:47.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mama... Mama is going to be all gone!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.32,0:08:49.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mama?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.08,0:08:51.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He means Sloth.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.30,0:08:54.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sloth is not your mama.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.12,0:08:56.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Homunculi do not have mothers.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.41,0:08:58.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Bring Mama back to life! Please!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.75,0:09:01.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't talk like you're human.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.93,0:09:03.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mama... Mama!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.81,0:09:05.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mama!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.55,0:09:06.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Envy!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.33,0:09:11.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.53,0:09:20.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you think \Nyou can do in your shape?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.10,0:09:32.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What power!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.14,0:09:36.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's only natural that \NEdward Elric would use Automail.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.22,0:09:37.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is fun!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.11,0:09:40.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Someone like you is a soldier?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.44,0:09:42.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That explains why no one has realized who the Führer is!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.23,0:09:47.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's still not too late for you. Become one of my soldiers.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.34,0:09:52.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We are ready to wage war on \Nthe north, the west, and the south.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.76,0:09:55.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The time has come for \Nthe continent to be united.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.15,0:09:57.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not interested.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.79,0:09:59.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In that case, die!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.17,0:10:11.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your pupils will be \Nfollowing you soon as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.25,0:10:16.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you doing?! \NI am your superior officer!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.63,0:10:19.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You too?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.76,0:10:21.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Izumi-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.00,0:10:23.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where's... Ed?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.17,0:10:27.10,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,By now, both brothers should be at the place that was written about in that journal.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.60,0:10:33.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You all believed... in those boys?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.53,0:10:38.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Believing in and protecting children \Nis the job of an adult.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.42,0:10:41.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's what someone once told me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.98,0:11:18.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.25,0:11:25.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.83,0:11:28.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You finally came.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.77,0:11:35.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now, that should \Nteach you a lesson.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.30,0:11:37.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't start any fights \Nwith these guys.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.07,0:11:42.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You really don't ever learn \Nunless you get hurt.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.68,0:11:44.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Something the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.96,0:11:48.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I think I just figured something out.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.52,0:11:50.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Figured what out?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.38,0:11:54.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hughes-san said something \Nbefore he died.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.66,0:11:57.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"What if everything was backwards?"
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.48,0:11:59.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I never understood what he meant.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.79,0:12:01.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And you figured it out?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.40,0:12:07.91,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,We've been thinking that the homunculi \Nwere trying to create a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.91,0:12:10.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But what if it was \Nthe other way around?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.34,0:12:14.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They wait until it is just barely completed, and then take it away.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.27,0:12:17.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then they eliminate everyone \Nwho can prove it ever happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.56,0:12:21.59,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,What's left is a rumor that says if you come near the Philosopher's Stone, you'll be destroyed.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.59,0:12:24.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In time, people become afraid of the Philosopher's Stone...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.42,0:12:28.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So they'll keep away from it?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.78,0:12:30.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But that would almost make them good people, wouldn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.89,0:12:34.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They're making sure people stay out of danger, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.78,0:12:36.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's more,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.90,0:12:38.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,no matter how dangerous it is,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.32,0:12:43.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll bet that people will \Nstill go on looking for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.17,0:12:47.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wonder how Edward-san and his brother are doing.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.92,0:12:49.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sure they're getting along fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.91,0:12:51.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That much is certain.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.79,0:12:56.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Pain that teaches a lesson, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.59,0:13:00.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But God is the only one who can teach that kind of lesson.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.93,0:13:08.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,R-Rose, what are you doing here?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.90,0:13:12.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've been waiting for you \Na long, long time.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.87,0:13:14.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed, I...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.65,0:13:16.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.77,0:13:22.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose, was Al brought here?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.83,0:13:24.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What exactly is this place?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.35,0:13:29.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My baby...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.74,0:13:36.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My baby...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.72,0:13:38.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You should have danced with her.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.97,0:13:42.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She's been waiting for you ever since we fled here.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.75,0:13:43.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're despicable.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.83,0:13:47.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lyra, you brought Rose here?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.84,0:13:51.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's an old city that \Nonly alchemists know of.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.33,0:13:53.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's what Dante-sensei told me.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.42,0:13:58.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Speaking of Dante-san, I still \Nhaven't heard how she was killed.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.67,0:14:01.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She was killed by \Nthat homunculus Greed.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.76,0:14:02.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I thought I told you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.98,0:14:04.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is a lie.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.79,0:14:05.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A lie?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.65,0:14:08.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The transmutation circle that was left in Dante-san's house
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.93,0:14:12.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,was one that could keep \Na homunculus from moving.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.38,0:14:16.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There were bones from the man \Non whom Greed was based.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.24,0:14:19.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Greed shouldn't have been able to \Ntake action against Dante-san.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.35,0:14:23.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you sure? \NStill, Dante-san definitely is dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.69,0:14:25.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But supposing that what was there
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.41,0:14:28.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,was nothing more than a shell \Nthat her soul had sloughed off...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.60,0:14:29.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you saying?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.93,0:14:33.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's suppose there were people who used the power of the Philosopher's Stone
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.98,0:14:36.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,to move from one body to another \Nand who have lived for hundreds of years.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.47,0:14:40.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Back there, you made it \Nlook like you were dead
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.52,0:14:44.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and then took over Lyra's body. \NIsn't that right?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.14,0:14:46.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed, stop! I am—
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.15,0:14:57.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was close.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.78,0:14:59.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When did you see the gate, Lyra?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.81,0:15:04.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You transmuted without \Nusing a transmutation circle.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.39,0:15:06.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's my answer, Dante!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.78,0:15:11.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When did you figure it out, \NEdward Elric?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.05,0:15:12.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then it's true?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.85,0:15:15.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've really come to like this body.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.50,0:15:17.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So then, what number is she?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.56,0:15:21.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who knows? \NIt hasn't been ten yet, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.19,0:15:25.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After all, I have to use the \NPhilosopher's Stone each time.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.45,0:15:29.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Did you wipe out the residents of this city to make your Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.76,0:15:33.72,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Yes, the same as with the nation to the east, \Nwhich was destroyed overnight.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.72,0:15:36.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I should mention, though, \Nthat I was not the one who made them.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.98,0:15:39.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hohenheim of Light...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.50,0:15:43.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You shouldn't address \Nyour own father like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.26,0:15:48.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So he's prolonged his life \Nthe same way? For what reason?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.30,0:15:50.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because we deserve to.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.67,0:15:53.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You covertly create \Nthe Philosopher's Stone
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.06,0:15:56.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,just so you can use it to extend your own lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.24,0:15:58.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You think you can \Nget away with that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.33,0:16:01.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Humans cannot use \Nthe Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.44,0:16:05.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that why, when people fail to \Ncomplete a Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.04,0:16:06.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,you obliterate everything \Nand leave behind the story
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.76,0:16:09.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that destruction befalls those who get too close to the Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.87,0:16:14.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, to keep people from getting \Ntoo close to the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.27,0:16:16.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And for those who \Nstill get too close,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.18,0:16:19.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,we take it from them at the last minute \Nand use it carefully.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.88,0:16:23.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After all, there's no telling what humans would do
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.24,0:16:25.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,if they were given a \NPhilosopher's Stone, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.73,0:16:30.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I do it to keep foolish people from destroying the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.63,0:16:34.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You could say that I have extended my life to protect the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.69,0:16:38.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,To keep humans from doing anything foolish with the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.56,0:16:41.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Cut the crap! You're human too!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.77,0:16:43.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.69,0:16:44.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lust!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.07,0:16:50.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lust! Where's Lust?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.71,0:16:50.48,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,What a shame.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.09,0:16:53.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was looking forward to entering this girl's body
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.23,0:16:57.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and making love to \NHohenheim's son.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.20,0:16:59.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose's body is next, is it?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.33,0:17:02.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes. I have obtained a \NPhilosopher's Stone again, and all.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.39,0:17:04.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al?! Where's Al?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.95,0:17:08.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where's Lust?! \NWhat happened to Lust?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.42,0:17:11.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Try asking him, Gluttony.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.52,0:17:12.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lust!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.65,0:17:16.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lust! Where's Lust?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.17,0:17:20.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She's dead. \NAnd it was my fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.39,0:17:23.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lust... is dead?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.04,0:17:27.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. Your pal Wrath sealed her up.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.42,0:17:35.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Gluttony?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.82,0:17:37.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lust...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.34,0:17:41.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Gluttony!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.79,0:17:42.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lust...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.70,0:17:46.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Here I come!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.80,0:18:01.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I knew it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.59,0:18:06.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Repeatedly bonding just your soul is not something you can continue doing forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.50,0:18:09.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Equivalent exchange!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.00,0:18:11.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's the backlash from performing that idiocy over and over!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.57,0:18:13.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Equivalent exchange?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.72,0:18:16.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you still believe in \Nthat childish theory?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.15,0:18:18.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's no theory! \NIt's the law of alchemy—
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.90,0:18:21.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,no, of the whole world!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.44,0:18:23.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're the one who \Nsaid so, aren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.56,0:18:27.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That in order to obtain anything, \Nit requires something of equal value?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.62,0:18:29.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's something that \Nonly a child would say.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.91,0:18:33.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Like "make everything equal," or "that wouldn't be fair."
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.21,0:18:37.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, there's no such thing as equivalent exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.30,0:18:38.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's absurd!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.70,0:18:42.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is a cost required in order for you to obtain something...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.06,0:18:43.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In that case, if you reverse it—
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.41,0:18:46.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,if you pay a price, you are certain to obtain something, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.27,0:18:50.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right. That's why people \Nput forth an effort to pay the price.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.29,0:18:52.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But there's something \Nstrange about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.11,0:18:55.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After all, even if you \Npay the same price,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.14,0:18:57.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,you can't always necessarily obtain the same thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.16,0:18:59.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, that's...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.00,0:19:03.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's the State Alchemist Exam, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.23,0:19:08.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to pass it, many people \Nspend time studying. That's a cost.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.95,0:19:12.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But only a handful of people \Nactually pass it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.55,0:19:15.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Everyone may start out the same \Nwhen they learn alchemy,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.72,0:19:18.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but huge differences arise in their actual abilities.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.47,0:19:22.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And people's lives \Nare not all equal, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.01,0:19:33.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If nobody does anything, \Nthat baby is going to die, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.24,0:19:34.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.14,0:19:37.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It really would be easy \Nfor me to kill it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.02,0:19:40.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If I do, was the baby \Nborn only in order to die?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.35,0:19:44.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The baby is paying the price of desperately trying to survive.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.65,0:19:48.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yet is death the only thing \Nthey're going to get for that?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.08,0:19:52.07,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Elsewhere, there are people who kill others \Nand continue to go on living.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.07,0:19:57.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No matter how hard you may try to live, when it's time for you to die, you die.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.06,0:20:00.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When you compare that to \Npeople who don't make any effort
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.12,0:20:03.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,yet are afforded riches and power \Nand live lives of happiness,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.04,0:20:05.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it's quite unfair, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.45,0:20:08.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The world is quite cruel.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.17,0:20:10.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Which is why you might say \Nit's so beautiful.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.37,0:20:11.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Cut the sophistry!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.21,0:20:19.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My baby...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.24,0:20:25.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Equivalent exchange is an excuse that the weak use to comfort themselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.99,0:20:30.67,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,They tell themselves that by paying a price, it's supposed to make themselves happier.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.67,0:20:33.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This baby doesn't \Nhave to make any excuses!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.74,0:20:36.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're his son, all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.91,0:20:49.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ouch...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.92,0:20:53.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is this? \NWhat's going on here?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.90,0:20:55.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My eyes...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.10,0:21:09.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.09,0:21:12.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.27,0:21:13.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward-kun!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.21,0:21:15.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you doing?! \NIt's an air raid!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.58,0:21:22.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hurry up!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.13,0:21:26.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wait! Pop, what are you doing here?! \NWhat is this place?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.47,0:21:30.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Pop"? Edward-kun, \Nwhat are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.72,0:21:33.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I thought you were at \NDante-san's place!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.34,0:21:35.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is this place?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.21,0:21:36.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's happened to me?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.73,0:21:39.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My face... my hand?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.26,0:21:45.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you my son Edward?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.91,0:21:47.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Of course I am!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.63,0:21:48.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you doing here?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.95,0:21:50.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't know...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.72,0:21:55.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's go! They're coming!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.16,0:21:57.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who do you mean, "they"?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.24,0:21:58.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Zeppelins!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.31,0:21:59.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Zeppelins?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.16,0:23:41.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:41.11,0:23:43.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 50: "Death"
